A||||4||JohnnyK||Charging/dying problem?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||01-08-2001||04:22 PM||||This is for my van, but it applies to both vehicles. A few days ago I tried to start my van, and it turned over 1 or twice and then completely died. I basically thought I just let it sit in the cold too long and jumped it. It ran fine for a few days. Today, i turned it off, and an hour later it did the same thing. The interior lights still work, but not enough juice to turn it over (I noticed that the window will only go down about an inch, stop, then I have to wait a few minutes, and it will do the same thing. Might just be the motor though). Is there an easy way to check the charging system? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiero Fanatic||01-09-2001||06:19 AM||||Test your alternator?||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||01-09-2001||12:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero Fanatic:<BR><B>Test your alternator?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>hook up a voltmeter to your battery, start it with everything (ac, lites, etc,) on you should show at least 13.5 volts up to 15. If it does, alt is working ok.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||01-09-2001||01:46 PM||||Yeah, did that today. Came out fine. Did a load test on my battery, and it seemed to fail. How would I check if the starter was taking a massive draw?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero Fanatic||01-14-2001||09:10 AM||||Have the starter tested also. Then test your ignition module in your distributor.||||reg||1
